:"concepts/attested-communication/what-is-a-card","title":"What is a Card?","description":"A Card is the basic unit of communication in AppKeyId. It is similar to a lightweight email, memo,","sidebar":"conceptsSidebar"},"concepts/attested-communication/what-is-attested-communication":{"id":"concepts/attested-communication/what-is-attested-communication","title":"What is Attested Communication","description":"Attested communication means that a communication event is not merely sent, opened, or clicked.","sidebar":"conceptsSidebar"},"concepts/attested-communication/why-acknowlegement":{"id":"concepts/attested-communication/why-acknowlegement","title":"Why Acknowledgements Matter","description":"Acknowledgements","sidebar":"conceptsSidebar"},"concepts/foundation/passkeys-explained":{"id":"concepts/foundation/passkeys-explained","title":"Passkeys Explained","description":"The emergence of FIDO2 passkeys changes what is possible.","sidebar":"conceptsSidebar"},"concepts/foundation/zero-trust-identity":{"id":"concepts/foundation/zero-trust-identity","title":"Zero Trust Identity","description":"AppKeyId applies Zero Trust principles to digital communication.","sidebar":"conceptsSidebar"},"concepts/intro":{"id":"concepts/intro","title":"Concepts","description":"Attested Communication is a new capability made possible by the widespread adoption of biometric","sidebar":"conceptsSidebar"},"concepts/use-cases/appkeyid-solution":{"id":"concepts/use-cases/appkeyid-solution","title":"AppKeyId is the solution","description":"AppKeyId Architecture","sidebar":"conceptsSidebar"},"concepts/use-cases/who-is-the-person":{"id":"concepts/use-cases/who-is-the-person","title":"Who Is the Person?","description":"Who are you really?","sidebar":"conceptsSidebar"},"concepts/use-cases/why-ai-breaks-digital":{"id":"concepts/use-cases/why-ai-breaks-digital","title":"Why AI Breaks Digital Trust","description":"Digital Trust","sidebar":"conceptsSidebar"},"concepts/use-cases/why-email-and-messaging":{"id":"concepts/use-cases/why-email-and-messaging","title":"Why Email and Messaging Aren't Enough","description":"Hacked Email & Sim Swap","sidebar":"conceptsSidebar"},"manual/cards/inbox":{"id":"manual/cards/inbox","title":"What is the Inbox","description":"<img","sidebar":"manualSidebar"},"manual/cards/outbox":{"id":"manual/cards/outbox","title":"What is the outbox","description":"The Outbox in the Cards tab contains all cards authored by the user. Cards are displayed","sidebar":"manualSidebar"},"manual/cardtypes/alibi":{"id":"manual/cardtypes/alibi","title":"Alibi Card","description":"Alibi Cards allow an AppKeyId user to create a verifiable digital record of where they were and when they were there.","sidebar":"manualSidebar"},"manual/cardtypes/capture":{"id":"manual/cardtypes/capture","title":"Capture Card","description":"Capture Cards solve a very common problem: you have a group of people and need to accurately collect their identity and contact information.","sidebar":"manualSidebar"},"manual/cardtypes/deck":{"id":"manual/cardtypes/deck","title":"Deck Card","description":"Decks extend the concept of AppKeyId Cards by arranging multiple Cards into an ordered sequence. Instead of presenting a single communication for acknowledgement, a Deck creates a progression in which each Card must be acknowledged before the next Card becomes available.","sidebar":"manualSidebar"},"manual/cardtypes/message":{"id":"manual/cardtypes/message","title":"Message Card","description":"Message cards are used for private messaging.","sidebar":"manualSidebar"},"manual/cardtypes/public":{"id":"manual/cardtypes/public","title":"Public Card","description":"Public Cards are designed to communicate information to a broad audience. Unlike private Message Cards,","sidebar":"manualSidebar"},"manual/cardtypes/public-deck":{"id":"manual/cardtypes/public-deck","title":"Public Deck Card","description":"","sidebar":"manualSidebar"},"manual/contacts/blocking":{"id":"manual/contacts/blocking","title":"Blocking Users","description":"","sidebar":"manualSidebar"},"manual/contacts/chatting":{"id":"manual/contacts/chatting","title":"Chatting with Contacts","description":"","sidebar":"manualSidebar"},"manual/contacts/contacts":{"id":"manual/contacts/contacts","title":"Managing Contacts","description":"","sidebar":"manualSidebar"},"manual/contacts/export":{"id":"manual/contacts/export","title":"Exporting Contacts","description":"","sidebar":"manualSidebar"},"manual/contacts/finding":{"id":"manual/contacts/finding","title":"Finding Contacts","description":"","sidebar":"manualSidebar"},"manual/contacts/inviting":{"id":"manual/contacts/inviting","title":"Inviting to AppKeyId","description":"","sidebar":"manualSidebar"},"manual/intro":{"id":"manual/intro","title":"Manual","description":"Welcome to the AppKeyId User Manual. This guide explains how to use AppKeyId to create, share,","sidebar":"manualSidebar"},"manual/profilemenu/logs":{"id":"manual/profilemenu/logs","title":"Logs","description":"","sidebar":"manualSidebar"},"manual/profilemenu/passkeys":{"id":"manual/profilemenu/passkeys","title":"AppKeyId Passkeys","description":"","sidebar":"manualSidebar"},"manual/profilemenu/profile":{"id":"manual/profilemenu/profile","title":"Profile","description":"Profile Picture","sidebar":"manualSidebar"},"manual/profilemenu/settings":{"id":"manual/profilemenu/settings","title":"AppKeyId Settings","description":"","sidebar":"manualSidebar"},"manual/teams/addmembers":{"id":"manual/teams/addmembers","title":"Add Team Members","description":"","sidebar":"manualSidebar"},"manual/teams/belongteam":{"id":"manual/teams/belongteam","title":"Teams I belong to","description":"","sidebar":"manualSidebar"},"manual/teams/capture":{"id":"manual/teams/capture","title":"Teams and Capture Cards","description":"","sidebar":"manualSidebar"},"manual/teams/createteam":{"id":"manual/teams/createteam","title":"Creating a Team","description":"","sidebar":"manualSidebar"},"manual/teams/export":{"id":"manual/teams/export","title":"Exporting Team Members","description":"","sidebar":"manualSidebar"},"manual/teams/properties":{"id":"manual/teams/properties","title":"Manage Team Properties","description":"","sidebar":"manualSidebar"},"selfhosted/intro":{"id":"selfhosted/intro","title":"Self-Hosted AppKeyId","description":"Overview","sidebar":"selfhostedSidebar"},"selfhosted/self-hosted-server/cryptographc-keys":{"id":"selfhosted/self-hosted-server/cryptographc-keys","title":"Cryptographic Keys and Repository Setup","description":"The AppKeyId Server uses public-key cryptography to secure its operations. Before building the server, you must obtain the source code and generate a pair of RSA keys.","sidebar":"selfhostedSidebar"},"selfhosted/self-hosted-server/environment":{"id":"selfhosted/self-hosted-server/environment","title":"Environment Variables Configuration","description":"The AppKeyId Server uses environment variables to configure its database connection, cryptographic keys, authentication services, and external integrations. These settings are stored in a file named .env, which Docker reads when starting the application.","sidebar":"selfhostedSidebar"},"selfhosted/self-hosted-server/launch-run":{"id":"selfhosted/self-hosted-server/launch-run","title":"Building and Running the AppKeyId Server","description":"With the environment variables configured, you are ready to build and start the AppKeyId Server.","sidebar":"selfhostedSidebar"},"selfhosted/self-hosted-server/prerequisite":{"id":"selfhosted/self-hosted-server/prerequisite","title":"Prerequisites and Installation","description":"Before building the AppKeyId Server, you need two tools: Docker to run the application in containers, and Node.js to build and manage the server software.","sidebar":"selfhostedSidebar"},"selfhosted/self-hosted-server/third-party":{"id":"selfhosted/self-hosted-server/third-party","title":"Configuring Third-Party Service Providers","description":"The AppKeyId Server relies on several external services for database storage, file attachments, SMS notifications, and email delivery. Before starting the server, you must configure these services and obtain the credentials needed to access them.","sidebar":"selfhostedSidebar"},"selfhosted/self-hosted-website/build-run":{"id":"selfhosted/self-hosted-website/build-run","title":"Build and Run the Website","description":"Once the configuration is complete, the website can be built and started using Docker Compose.","sidebar":"selfhostedSidebar"},"selfhosted/self-hosted-website/configure-website":{"id":"selfhosted/self-hosted-website/configure-website","title":"AppKeyId Self-Hosted Website","description":"Installation and Configuration Guide","sidebar":"selfhostedSidebar"},"tutorial/intro":{"id":"tutorial/intro","title":"Tutorial Intro","description":"Welcome to the AppKeyId tutorial. This guide will walk you through the basic steps of using AppKeyId to create and share attested communication cards.","sidebar":"tutorialSidebar"},"tutorial/tutorial-basics/create-first-card":{"id":"tutorial/tutorial-basics/create-first-card","title":"Creating Your First Card","description":"Now that your AppKeyId account is ready, you can begin using it to share and acknowledge information.","sidebar":"tutorialSidebar"},"tutorial/tutorial-basics/signup-to-appkeyid":{"id":"tutorial/tutorial-basics/signup-to-appkeyid","title":"Signing Up with Email","description":"This tutorial walks you through the process of creating a new AppKeyId account. AppKeyId uses FIDO2 passkeys to authenticate users and protect account access with biometric verification.","sidebar":"tutorialSidebar"},"tutorial/tutorial-basics/signup-using-apple":{"id":"tutorial/tutorial-basics/signup-using-apple","title":"Signing Up with Apple ID","description":"This tutorial walks you through the process of creating a new AppKeyId account using Sign in with Apple.","sidebar":"tutorialSidebar"},"tutorial/tutorial-basics/signup-using-google":{"id":"tutorial/tutorial-basi